	&lt;/head>
  &lt;body>
    &lt;p>
&lt;b>Usage of Context is mismatched between XMI and RDF versions of the MVF specification       
&lt;/b>&lt;br>This diagram shows all the MVF&amp;#160;concepts relating the term context (which has two different definitions and highlights how the mismatch might be resolved.

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
The &lt;span style="color:#cc00cc;">purple text&lt;/span> highlights properties (association ends) relevant to the representation of Context in the RDF-based&amp;#160;ontologies imported by &lt;a href="https://www.omg.org/spec/MVF/20220501/AboutMVF.rdf">https://www.omg.org/spec/MVF/20220501/AboutMVF.rdf&lt;/a>

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
The &lt;span style="color:#ff0000;">red text&lt;/span> indicates the closest equivalent in the metamodel representation of MVF&amp;#160;in XMI and PDF&amp;#160;specifications. There are two identified mismatches:

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
&amp;#160;

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;p>
Type

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;ul>
      &lt;li>
In the RDF&amp;#160;ontologies, &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1686253385870_540454_6985" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="NO_UPDATE">context&lt;/a> is a class defined by the &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1686253385729_992221_5851" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="AUTOMATIC_UPDATE">Commons Contextual Designators Ontology&lt;/a>

      &lt;/li>
      &lt;li>
In the XMI&amp;#160;metamodel, &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1685901462397_533420_5018" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="NO_UPDATE">context&lt;/a> is a UML role of &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1685901462397_174463_4991" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="NO_UPDATE">MVFEntry&lt;/a>

      &lt;/li>
    &lt;/ul>
    &lt;p>
Definition

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;ul>
      &lt;li>
In the RDF, &lt;a href="mdel://_19_0_4_c480314_1686253385870_540454_6985" erit:display="NAME" erit:update="NO_UPDATE">context&lt;/a> is defined as: &amp;quot;&lt;i>situation or frame of reference in which something applies, exists, happens, or is used and that helps to illustrate or explain it&lt;/i>&amp;quot;

      &lt;/li>
      &lt;li>
In the PDF context is defined as:&amp;#160;&amp;quot;&lt;i>Link to another MVFEntry that provides context for this MVFEntry&lt;/i>&amp;quot; (Note: the XMI&amp;#160;does not include a definition but is intended to be equivalent to the PDF&amp;#160;metamodel)

      &lt;/li>
    &lt;/ul>
    &lt;p>
Source

    &lt;/p>

    &lt;ul>
      &lt;li>
RDF&amp;#160;definition cites a source for the definition and usage i.e. ISO&amp;#160;1179-3

      &lt;/li>
      &lt;li>
PDF&amp;#160;does not cite a source

      &lt;/li>
    &lt;/ul>
&lt;/body>
